{% extends "layout.njk" %}
{% import "macros.njk" as m %}
{% set title = "Community site sections" %}
{% set slug = "patterns-community" %}

{% block content %}
<h1>Community site sections</h1>
<p class="lede">
  Sections from
  <a href="https://lzr.life" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">lzr.life</a>,
  a volunteer group's zine library, rebuilt in the class build. The sections,
  headings, labels and links are the site's. Longer body text is shortened, and
  the layout inside each section is a plain arrangement of framework pieces
  rather than a copy of the site's styling. Images are placeholders. The rules
  behind them are on <a href="./composition.html">Composition</a>.
</p>

<section id="nav">
  <h2>Navigation</h2>
  <p>
    A home link and the five sections of the site.
  </p>
  {% set classless %}
<nav class="navbar">
  <div class="navbar-start">
    <a href="#" class="semantic" aria-label="Home"><strong>LZR</strong></a>
  </div>
  <div class="navbar-end" style="flex-wrap: wrap">
    <a href="#" class="link">Zines</a>
    <a href="#" class="link">How To</a>
    <a href="#" class="link">Events</a>
    <a href="#" class="link">LZR in the Wild</a>
    <a href="#" class="link">Get in Touch</a>
  </div>
</nav>
  {% endset %}
  {{ m.demo("community-nav", classless) }}
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Layout:</strong> <code>.navbar-end</code> is a flex row, so with five links it needs <code>flex-wrap: wrap</code> to survive a phone.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="welcome">
  <h2>Welcome</h2>
  <p>
    The home page opens with the group's name, a few short lines, a quote, and
    one button into the catalog.
  </p>
  {% set classless %}
<section class="prose">
  <h2>Little Zine Revolution</h2>
  <p>Welcome!</p>
  <p>Here at the Little Zine Revolution, we curate and distribute anti-colonial zines.</p>
  <p>Little actions have ripple effects.</p>
  <p>Zines are like little love notes.</p>
  <p>Revolution is love.</p>
  <blockquote>
    <p>You have to act as if it were possible to radically transform the world. And you have to do it all the time.</p>
    <small class="text-secondary">Angela Davis</small>
  </blockquote>
  <a href="#" role="button" class="btn">Explore the Zine Catalog</a>
</section>
  {% endset %}
  {{ m.demo("community-welcome", classless) }}
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Text:</strong> one <code>.prose</code> spaces the short lines, the quote and the button. Each line is its own paragraph, so each gets the same <code>1rem</code> beat.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="how-to-help">
  <h2>How to help</h2>
  <p>
    On the home page, a short version of the how-to guide: three headed
    paragraphs, each linking to its part of the full guide.
  </p>
  {% set classless %}
<section class="prose">
  <h2>How to Help</h2>
  <p>Print! Fold! Distribute! <a href="#" class="link">Read the how-to guide</a>.</p>
  <h3>Printing</h3>
  <p>Find a zine in the <a href="#" class="link">zine catalog</a>, then see the <a href="#" class="link">printing tips</a>.</p>
  <h3>Folding</h3>
  <p>Come to an event, or fold on your own with the <a href="#" class="link">folding instructions</a>.</p>
  <h3>Distribution</h3>
  <p>Leave them where people will find them. See the <a href="#" class="link">distribution guide</a>.</p>
</section>
  {% endset %}
  {{ m.demo("community-how-to-help", classless) }}
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Text:</strong> this is all prose: headings and paragraphs with inline links. The links point at anchors on the how-to page, so the full guide has the same three headings.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="catalog">
  <h2>Zine catalog</h2>
  <p>
    A search field, the topics to filter by, and the zines as linked titles with
    their cover images. Topics combine, so they are checkboxes here.
  </p>
  {% set classless %}
<form>
  <label class="label">
    <p>Search</p>
    <input class="input" type="search" />
  </label>
  <fieldset class="fieldset">
    <legend class="fieldset-legend">Topics</legend>
    <div class="flex" style="flex-wrap: wrap">
      <label class="label"><input type="checkbox" class="checkbox" /> color</label>
      <label class="label"><input type="checkbox" class="checkbox" /> double sided</label>
      <label class="label"><input type="checkbox" class="checkbox" checked /> single sided</label>
      <label class="label"><input type="checkbox" class="checkbox" /> trifold</label>
      <label class="label"><input type="checkbox" class="checkbox" /> quarters</label>
    </div>
  </fieldset>
</form>

<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(9rem, 1fr)); gap: var(--padding)">
  <a href="#" class="semantic">
    <div style="aspect-ratio: 3 / 4; background: var(--surface-strong); border-radius: var(--border-radius); margin-bottom: calc(var(--padding) / 2)"></div>
    <span class="link">18mr for the Love of Bread</span>
  </a>
  <a href="#" class="semantic">
    <div style="aspect-ratio: 3 / 4; background: var(--surface-strong); border-radius: var(--border-radius); margin-bottom: calc(var(--padding) / 2)"></div>
    <span class="link">Anarchist Compass</span>
  </a>
  <a href="#" class="semantic">
    <div style="aspect-ratio: 3 / 4; background: var(--surface-strong); border-radius: var(--border-radius); margin-bottom: calc(var(--padding) / 2)"></div>
    <span class="link">Butterfly</span>
  </a>
  <a href="#" class="semantic">
    <div style="aspect-ratio: 3 / 4; background: var(--surface-strong); border-radius: var(--border-radius); margin-bottom: calc(var(--padding) / 2)"></div>
    <span class="link">Cointelpro</span>
  </a>
</div>
  {% endset %}
  {{ m.demo("community-catalog", classless) }}
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Controls:</strong> each checkbox is a <code>.label</code> row, and the <code>.fieldset</code> names the group once with its legend. The labels keep their bottom margin, which also spaces them when the row wraps.</li>
    <li><strong>Actions:</strong> each zine is one link. <code>.semantic</code> strips the anchor and the title inside is marked <code>.link</code>, so the cover and title click as one target.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="zine">
  <h2>Zine page</h2>
  <p>
    One zine: its cover, what kind of zine it is, its tag, and the PDF to preview
    or download. Beside it on the site sits the studio's credit card, shown
    further down this page.
  </p>
  {% set classless %}
<article class="flex flip">
  <div style="flex: 0 0 12rem; aspect-ratio: 3 / 4; background: var(--surface-strong); border-radius: var(--border-radius)" role="img" aria-label="Butterfly cover"></div>
  <div class="prose" style="flex: 1">
    <h2>Butterfly</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary">Single-sided, 8-page mini zine · Inspiration</p>
    <p><span class="badge">Single Sided</span></p>
    <div class="flex" style="flex-wrap: wrap">
      <a href="#" role="button" class="btn">Download PDF</a>
      <a href="#" role="button" class="btn btn-secondary">Preview</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</article>
  {% endset %}
  {{ m.demo("community-zine", classless) }}
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Text:</strong> the format and category are <code>.text-secondary</code>; the tag is a <code>.badge</code>, the same tag the catalog filters on.</li>
    <li><strong>Actions:</strong> download is the filled button because it is why the visitor came; preview is secondary.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="events">
  <h2>Events and calendar subscription</h2>
  <p>
    The events page lists upcoming events in date order and offers the whole
    calendar as a subscription. There were no upcoming events when this was
    written, so only the subscription block is shown.
  </p>
  {% set classless %}
<section class="prose">
  <h2>Events</h2>
  <p>Check out the upcoming events below, or subscribe to get every event, including future ones.</p>
  <div class="flex" style="flex-wrap: wrap">
    <a href="#" class="link">Apple / Outlook</a>
    <a href="#" class="link">Google Calendar</a>
    <a href="#" class="link">Download ICS file</a>
  </div>
</section>
  {% endset %}
  {{ m.demo("community-events", classless) }}
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Actions:</strong> three equal choices, so they are links in a <code>.flex</code> row rather than buttons competing for attention.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="community-kit">
  <h2>Community kit</h2>
  <p>
    Downloadable branding, so anyone starting their own little zine revolution
    can match it. Each item is a picture and its file links.
  </p>
  {% set classless %}
<section class="prose">
  <h2>Community Kit</h2>
  <p>Share the love!</p>
</section>
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(12rem, 1fr)); gap: var(--padding)">
  <article class="card-border">
    <div style="aspect-ratio: 1; background: var(--surface-strong); border-radius: var(--border-radius); margin-bottom: calc(var(--padding) / 2)"></div>
    <strong>QR Codes</strong>
    <p class="flex"><a href="#" class="link">PNG</a> <a href="#" class="link">SVG</a></p>
  </article>
  <article class="card-border">
    <div style="aspect-ratio: 1; background: var(--surface-strong); border-radius: var(--border-radius); margin-bottom: calc(var(--padding) / 2)"></div>
    <strong>Logos</strong>
    <p class="flex"><a href="#" class="link">Logo</a> <a href="#" class="link">Dark</a> <a href="#" class="link">B&amp;W</a></p>
  </article>
  <article class="card-border">
    <div style="aspect-ratio: 1; background: var(--surface-strong); border-radius: var(--border-radius); margin-bottom: calc(var(--padding) / 2)"></div>
    <strong>Tags</strong>
    <p class="flex"><a href="#" class="link">PDF</a> <a href="#" class="link">SVG</a> <a href="#" class="link">Page PDF</a></p>
  </article>
  <article class="card-border">
    <div style="aspect-ratio: 1; background: var(--surface-strong); border-radius: var(--border-radius); margin-bottom: calc(var(--padding) / 2)"></div>
    <strong>Signs</strong>
    <p class="flex"><a href="#" class="link">PDF</a> <a href="#" class="link">SVG</a> <a href="#" class="link">Page PDF</a></p>
  </article>
  <article class="card-border">
    <div style="aspect-ratio: 1; background: var(--surface-strong); border-radius: var(--border-radius); margin-bottom: calc(var(--padding) / 2)"></div>
    <strong>Quartersheet Flyers</strong>
    <p class="flex"><a href="#" class="link">SVG</a> <a href="#" class="link">PDF</a></p>
  </article>
  <article class="card-border">
    <div style="aspect-ratio: 1; background: var(--surface-strong); border-radius: var(--border-radius); margin-bottom: calc(var(--padding) / 2)"></div>
    <strong>Lazers</strong>
    <p class="flex"><a href="#" class="link">Favicon SVG</a></p>
  </article>
</div>
  {% endset %}
  {{ m.demo("community-kit", classless) }}
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Surface:</strong> six items of equal weight, so <code>.card-border</code> rather than raised cards.</li>
    <li><strong>Layout:</strong> the file links in each item are a <code>.flex</code> row; the <code>1rem</code> gap keeps short labels like PDF and SVG from running together.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="gallery">
  <h2>LZR in the Wild</h2>
  <p>
    Photos of zine displays out in coffee shops, bookstores and little free
    libraries. A plain grid of images.
  </p>
  {% set classless %}
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(10rem, 1fr)); gap: calc(var(--padding) / 2)">
  {% for alt in ["Zine bin at a coffee shop", "Display at a bookstore", "Little free library", "Free pantry shelf", "Convenience store counter", "Anime cafe display"] %}
  <div style="aspect-ratio: 1; background: var(--surface-strong); border-radius: var(--border-radius)" role="img" aria-label="{{ alt }}"></div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
  {% endset %}
  {{ m.demo("community-gallery", classless) }}
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Layout:</strong> a tighter gap than the rest of the site, half of <code>--padding</code>, so the photos read as one wall rather than as separate items.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="get-in-touch">
  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>
    No form: a line setting expectations and two ways to reach the group.
  </p>
  {% set classless %}
<section class="prose">
  <h2>Get in Touch</h2>
  <p>Please be patient. We are a tiny team!</p>
  <div class="flex" style="flex-wrap: wrap">
    <a href="#" class="link">Follow us on Instagram</a>
    <a href="#" class="link">Send us an email</a>
  </div>
</section>
  {% endset %}
  {{ m.demo("community-get-in-touch", classless) }}
</section>

<section id="credit">
  <h2>"Want a site like this?"</h2>
  <p>
    The studio's credit, at the foot of most pages and beside each zine. It is
    the only block on the site in someone else's colours.
  </p>
  {% set classless %}
<aside class="card-border retheme prose" style="--primary: rebeccapurple">
  <h3>Want a site like this?</h3>
  <p>We build accessible, performant sites your users will love.</p>
  <a href="#" role="button" class="btn">Book a free call</a>
</aside>
  {% endset %}
  {{ m.demo("community-credit", classless) }}
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Boundary:</strong> <code>.retheme</code> with the studio's <code>--primary</code> recolours the button, border and text inside the block and nothing outside it.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="footer">
  <h2>Footer</h2>
  <p>
    Contact links, the full site map, and the disclaimer.
  </p>
  {% set classless %}
<footer>
  <hr class="divider" />
  <div class="flex" style="flex-wrap: wrap">
    <a href="#" class="link">Follow us on Instagram</a>
    <a href="#" class="link">Send us an email</a>
  </div>
  <nav class="flex" style="flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: var(--padding)">
    <a href="#" class="link">Home</a>
    <a href="#" class="link">How to Help</a>
    <a href="#" class="link">Zine Catalog</a>
    <a href="#" class="link">Events</a>
    <a href="#" class="link">LZR in the Wild</a>
    <a href="#" class="link">Community Kit</a>
    <a href="#" class="link">Get in Touch</a>
    <a href="#" class="link">Sites that inspire us</a>
  </nav>
  <p class="text-secondary" style="margin-top: var(--padding)">
    <small>This is a platform for independent voices. Zines are the responsibility of their creators and are not endorsed by this site.</small>
  </p>
</footer>
  {% endset %}
  {{ m.demo("community-footer", classless) }}
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Spacing:</strong> nothing here is in <code>.prose</code>, so the groups are spaced with <code>margin-top: var(--padding)</code>, top margins being the one thing the framework never sets.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
{% endblock %}
